entries.content:
Here is a brief information about the relationship of current employees:

Vergilius: emotionally detached from most of the group. Has a soft spot for Charon. Considers Dante as some sort of confidant;

Charon: Disconnected from the group and shows no interest in becoming close with them. Contacts only with Vergilius;

Dante: Gets along with Rodion, Gregor and Don Quixote. Receives support and obedience from Outis. Afraid of Ryōshū and Heathcliff;

Yi Sang: Has little contact with others of his own will, as he is more immersed in himself;

Faust: Of all the employees, Faust has a warmer attitude only to Dante. Neutral to the rest;

Don Quixote: Tries to get along with everyone, but gets along especially well with Dante, Rodion and Sinclair;

Ryōshū: Not interested in building contacts with others;

Meursault: Not interested in building contacts with others. Loyal and obedient to Dante;

Hong Lu: Tries to get along with everyone;

Heathcliff: Doesn't get along well with everyone except Meursault. Especially complex relations with Ishmael;

Ishmael: Neutral in relation to almost everyone. Especially complex relations with Heathcliff;

Rodion: Tries to get along with everyone, but gets along especially well with Gregor, Don Quixote and Sinclair. Cares about Sinclair much;

Sinclair: Neutral in relation to almost everyone. Gets along with Gregor, Don Quixote and Rodion;

Outis: Cold to everyone, except for Dante, with whom she has a noticeable sycophantic relationship;

Gregor: Tries to get along with everyone, but gets along especially well with Dante, Rodion and Sinclair.

